# CODEOWNERS — {{PROJECT_NAME}}
#
# Maps repository paths to the people responsible for reviewing them, so every part of the
# project has an owner. GitHub requests a review from the listed owners when a pull request
# touches a matching path. On its own this file only *requests* reviews; it blocks nothing
# unless branch protection on {{DEFAULT_BRANCH}} requires code-owner review (see
# docs/governance/GOVERNANCE.md, "Decision-making", for the branch protection command).
#
# The handles below are placeholders of the form @org/<role>; replace them with the people or
# teams named in docs/governance/CHARTER.md. Later entries win, so order general to specific.

# Default owner: the project manager catches anything not matched below.
*                         @org/project-manager

# Data, schema and lookups: the data engineer; meaning: the subject-matter expert.
/data/                    @org/data-engineer
/data/lookups/            @org/data-engineer @org/subject-matter-expert
/docs/data-dictionary.md  @org/subject-matter-expert

# Pipeline code: the engineer owns the data flow, the developer the tooling around it.
/scripts/                 @org/data-engineer @org/software-developer
/pipelines/               @org/data-engineer @org/software-developer
/tests/                   @org/software-developer

# Documentation carries meaning, so the subject-matter expert reviews it.
/docs/                    @org/subject-matter-expert

# Governance, the charter and the data-management plan set the project's terms.
/docs/governance/         @org/project-manager @org/legal

# Environment and CI affect reproducibility for everyone.
/pyproject.toml           @org/software-developer
/uv.lock                  @org/software-developer
/.github/                 @org/software-developer
